WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.069
-The White House
released a damning memo

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.838
from President Trump's call
with the leader of Ukraine

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.608
after the House opened
a formal impeachment inquiry.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.910
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.380
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.883
After Democrats
announced yesterday

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.817
they would move forward
with impeachment,

00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:21.321
the White House announced
that they would release notes

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.656
of Trump's phone call
with Ukraine's president

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.026
in which Trump pressured him to
interfere in the 2020 election

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.562
by digging up dirt on Joe Biden
and his son.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.497
And suddenly everyone
started speculating

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.699
that maybe --
maybe the transcript

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.501
wouldn't be as bad
as we were expecting.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:40.439
-I just don't understand
why you do it today

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.977
when the transcript
theoretically -- I'm not say --

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:47.580
could be somewhat exculpatory
of Trump.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.116
-If the transcript
is exculpatory --

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.685
that's sort of legalese
for helpful to the president.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.020
-Well, my first thought
is that President Trump

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.790
would not release
this transcript

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.190
if it were not exculpatory.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.225
-Yes, he would.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.694
Donald Trump
is literally incapable

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.663
of doing anything exculpatory.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.698
First of all,
he would have to know

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.667
what the word
"exculpatory" means.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.303
"Of course I know
what 'exculpatory' means.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.940
It means you used to be
culpatory."

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.475
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.109
And he certainly couldn't
pronounce it.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.413
I mean, yesterday, he couldn't
even read the word "tire"

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.681
off a teleprompter.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:28.454
-Americans will never fire
or tire in our effort.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.990
-Oh, my God, he couldn't read
a one-syllable word.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.560
And I love the irony of saying
"Americans will never tire"

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.994
while you're standing there
looking like

00:01:35.994 --> 00:01:39.598
you just drank a bottle
of NyQuil during a gas leak.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:46.705
"Americans will never tire or --
or fire."

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:49.843
I love that thing he does where
instead of correcting himself,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.410
he acts like both words
were right.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.013
Like he's reading
a Dr. Seuss book.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:02:00.086
"Americans will never fire or
tire or get stuck in the mire,

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:05.424
but they'll definitely hire
a liar who perspires."

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.994
So at first some people thought
the notes from the phone call

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.795
would somehow clear Trump
of wrongdoing,

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.164
and then there was the question

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.699
of whether this supposed
transcript will even be complete

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:14.900
because as we all know,

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.902
White House transcripts
have been edited before.

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:18.838
I mean, remember,
this is the guy

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.973
who literally doctored
a hurricane map

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:23.676
by drawing a circle in Sharpie
to include Alabama.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.777
There was a good chance

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.645
the supposed transcript
would come out

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:29.382
and the first line would be
the president of Ukraine saying,

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.884
"Thanks for being
so innocent, sir."

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.320
Then there's the fact
that actual transcripts

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.422
of Trump's words
are often incomplete

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.591
because even the world's best
stenographers

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.192
have no idea what he's saying,

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:41.694
like the time
the Associated Press

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.662
put out a transcript
of an interview with Trump

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.698
and there were sentences
where even the reporters

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.400
could not understand
what he was saying.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.103
These are sentences
from the actual transcript.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.670
"Here's part of your story.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.506
It's going to be
a big unintelligible.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.808
I'll tell you the other thing is
unintelligible.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.310
We've been working on it.
Unintelligible.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.680
Secretary Mnuchin
is a very talented person,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.048
very smart, very successful,
unintelligible.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:06.686
Let me leave a little room
just in case unintelligible."

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:10.222
My God, "Unintelligible" should
be his Secret Service code name.

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.959
"Unintelligible is on the move.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.693
He said he was going
to McDernald's,

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.896
but we think he means
McDonald's."

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.299
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.769
And then, of course,
Trump himself

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:26.005
was going around
insisting repeatedly

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:28.807
that he did not pressure
the president of Ukraine

00:03:28.807 --> 00:03:31.377
to investigate a political rival
in exchange

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:34.313
for hundreds of millions
of dollars in military aid.

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:37.350
-It was a totally appropriate
conversation.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.785
It was actually
a beautiful conversation.

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:43.556
There was no quid pro quo.
There was nothing.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.725
It was a perfect conversation.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.994
The conversation, by the way,
was absolutely perfect.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:52.531
It was a beautiful,
warm, nice conversation.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:55.768
The conversation I had
with the president of Ukraine

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.870
was absolutely perfect.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.041
The conversation I had
with the president of Ukraine

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.109
was absolutely a 10.

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:05.244
It was perfect.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.413
-A 10?

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.415
Why are you talking about
a phone call

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.917
like you're creeping on women
at the beach?

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:13.519
"That call is a 10.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.989
Wait until you hear the jugs
on that call."

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.323
So there you go.

00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:20.593
The media speculated that
the call would be exculpatory,

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.328
impeachment calls
would be premature,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.396
and Trump said it would prove
he was innocent.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.899
They all said, "There's no way
Trump would be dumb enough

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.569
to release a transcript in which
he commits a bunch of crimes,

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:32.004
like asking for
a personal political favor

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:33.272
in exchange for hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:34.673
in military aid."

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:37.076
And then this morning, Trump
released notes from the call

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.178
in which it turns out
he was dumb enough

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.580
to commit a bunch of crimes,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.749
like asking for
a personal political favor

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.784
in exchange for hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:45.752
in military aide.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.353
-Here's what the president said.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.555
"There's a lot of talk
about Biden's son,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.490
that Biden stopped
the prosecution,

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.993
and a lot of people want
to find out about that,

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:57.530
so whatever you can do with the
Attorney General would be great.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.800
Biden went around bragging
that he stopped the prosecution.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.070
So if you can look into it,
it sounds horrible to me."

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.706
-The first investigation
that the president brings up

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.274
with the president of Ukraine --

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.775
This is immediately following

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.378
the Ukrainian president's
mention of military aid

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.846
and how he wants to continue
with military aid

00:05:14.846 --> 00:05:17.549
from the United States,
which we know at this point,

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.919
a large portion of which
had been suspended.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.287
Here's what the president says

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.955
in response
to that conversation.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.724
"I would like to ask you
to do us a favor, though,

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.094
because our country
has been through a lot.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:30.229
Ukraine knows a lot about it."

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.798
-In an official call with the
president of another country,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.567
he literally brought up
Joe Biden, Rudy Giuliani,

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.870
and said the words "I would
like you to do us a favor."

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.039
It doesn't get more obvious
than that.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.041
It actually would have
been better for Trump

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:45.845
if the whole transcript had
just said "unintelligible."

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.680
At when Trump asks
for the favor,

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.615
it wasn't just
an innocent request.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.949
As this call was happening,

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:53.352
Trump was holding up hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:54.620
in military aid to Ukraine

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.789
that Ukraine desperately wanted
from the U.S.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.726
In fact, Trump specifically
brought up the Biden stuff

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.527
right after
the Ukrainian president

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.929
brought up that military aid.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.796
In the memo,
the Ukrainian president said,

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:06.232
"I would also like to thank you

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:08.434
for your great support
in the area of defense."

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:11.103
And then the very next sentence
out of Trump's mouth was,

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.239
"I would like you
to do us a favor, though."

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.675
That is an obvious quid pro quo.

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.343
The only way
it's not a quid pro quo

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.278
is that when it comes
to committing crimes,

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.579
Trump is definitely not a pro.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.381
He's an idiot.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:25.250
It's more like a quid idiot quo.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.053
He literally said, "I'd like you
to do us a favor."

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:30.022
He might as well have been
having this meeting

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.958
at his daughter's wedding
while petting a cat.

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:36.062
Or if not a cat,
one of his other pets.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.763
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:42.134
Let's remember --
Let's remember Rudy Giuliani

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.870
was a private citizen,
the president's personal lawyer,

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:48.241
who was on a fishing expedition
to concoct a fake scandal

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.142
and get Ukraine
to manufacture dirt

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:51.810
on a political opponent,
Joe Biden.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.379
The fact that his name came up

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.280
on this call even once
is insane,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.883
but look how many times
Trump mentioned Rudy.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.886
"Mr. Giuliani's
a highly respected man.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.887
He was the mayor
of New York City, great mayor.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.388
And I would like him
to call you.

00:07:03.388 --> 00:07:05.991
I will ask him to call you,
along with the Attorney General.

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:08.127
Rudy very much knows
what's happening

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.728
and he's a very capable guy."

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:10.596
But he's not.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.665
He does not know
what's happening

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.667
and he is definitely
not a capable guy.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.902
For one thing,
any time he does a interview,

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:18.871
he looks like a guy
in a haunted house

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.140
after a zombie just popped out
of the bushes.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.241
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:24.577
In fact, Rudy has spent
the last few days

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.378
spitting out live
on national television.

00:07:26.378 --> 00:07:28.080
First he tried out
some prop comedy

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.316
by showing everyone his phone
in a Fox interview

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:33.486
and then showing up to another
Fox interview reading a book.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:36.856
Why?
Why's he doing prop comedy now.

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.390
"Here's a phone.
Here's a book.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:42.128
And here's one of my puppets.
He's actually my brother."

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:45.764
Also, I can assure you, Rudy
is not a highly respected man.

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:46.999
In fact,
just to give you an idea

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.601
of how little he's respected
on Capitol Hill,

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:51.404
Politico reported today that,
and this is real,

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:53.406
"At the House Democratic meeting
this morning,

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:55.240
Rudy Giuliani was the butt
of a joke.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.477
Congressman Hakeem Jeffries
showed a Seth Meyers sizzle reel

00:07:58.477 --> 00:08:00.879
of Giuliani's recent
cable appearances.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.182
The room erupted in laughter."

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.284
That's right,
as House Democrats --

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.186
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.256
As they were meeting

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:12.858
to discuss impeaching the
president of the United States,

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:16.262
they were watching a sizzle
reel of our Rudy Giuliani jokes.

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:22.000
Does that mean I could get
called as an official witness

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.168
in the impeachment?

00:08:23.168 --> 00:08:24.837
Oh, my God
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:30.443
I mean, I already have
my testimony prepared.

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:33.746
"Yes, Mr. Chairman,
while I do not have any insights

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:36.649
into Mr. Giuliani's
conversations with Ukraine,

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.951
I can confirm that he does,
in fact,

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:41.620
look like he accidentally
stuck his [bleep]

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.855
in an electrical socket."

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.358
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.398 --> 00:08:54.834
"Yes, you heard me right."

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:55.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.235
So you got the president

00:08:57.235 --> 00:09:00.139
dangling a quid pro quo
asking for a political favor

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.040
and repeatedly prodding
a foreign leader

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.642
to speak with
his personal lawyer

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:06.679
and manufacture a baseless smear
of a political opponent.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:08.747
Just what we can see
in this memo alone

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:10.048
is impeachable behavior,

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:12.684
let alone what's in the full
whistle-blower complaint.

00:09:12.684 --> 00:09:14.186
I mean, can you imagine how bad

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.055
that full whistle-blower
report is?

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.723
What else could it possibly say?

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:20.426
"After the call, Mr. Trump then
stood up, tripped on his tie,

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:23.328
fell headfirst into a garbage
can, got up, ran into a wall,

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:25.731
knocked himself unconscious,
woke up, and screamed,

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.699
'Where am I,
and who [bleep] my pants?'"

00:09:27.699 --> 00:09:30.435
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:09:30.435 --> 00:09:33.038
Today...

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:36.041
Today Trump actually met
with the president of Ukraine

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:38.277
on the sidelines
of the United Nations

00:09:38.277 --> 00:09:39.778
and claimed he hadn't
pressured him

00:09:39.778 --> 00:09:42.481
while also insisting all he
cared about was corruption.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:44.183
-You know what?
There was no pressure.

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:47.319
And, by the way, you know
there was no pressure.

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:50.188
All you have to do is see it,
what went on on the call.

00:09:50.188 --> 00:09:51.923
-Would you like
President Zelensky

00:09:51.923 --> 00:09:54.126
to do more on Joe Biden
and the investigation?

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:57.863
-No, I want him to do
whatever he can

00:09:57.863 --> 00:10:00.098
but whatever he can do
in terms of corruption

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:01.934
because the corruption
is massive.

00:10:01.934 --> 00:10:04.003
-Oh, you want him to do
something with corruption?

00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:05.871
Okay, well, he's sitting
right next to you.

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:08.207
Did he bring his handcuffs?

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:09.708
'Cause when it comes
to stopping corruption,

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:10.742
one thing's for sure.

00:10:10.742 --> 00:10:12.344
The president of Ukraine
will never...

00:10:12.344 --> 00:10:17.216
-Fire or tire.

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:20.052
-Now, one big question looming
over the impeachment debate

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:21.988
has always been
the political impact.

00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:24.390
How would it affect Trump's
chances of getting reelected?

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.059
Would it cut into his chances,
or would it solidify his base?

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:29.428
Some Democrats have been scared
that impeachment

00:10:29.428 --> 00:10:31.896
would somehow be good for him
or play into his hands.

00:10:31.896 --> 00:10:33.265
We have to drop this idea

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.768
that Trump is playing
three-dimensional chess.

00:10:35.768 --> 00:10:38.169
He's more like a guy
who ate a chess piece,

00:10:38.169 --> 00:10:39.404
is now choking on it,

00:10:39.404 --> 00:10:42.174
and instead of gesturing
for the Heimlich maneuver,

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:46.578
eats another chess piece
to dislodge the first one.

00:10:46.578 --> 00:10:48.714
In fact, Trump himself
has made this argument,

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.015
that he wants to be impeached

00:10:50.015 --> 00:10:52.417
because it would somehow be good
for him politically.

00:10:52.417 --> 00:10:54.519
In fact, he repeated that claim
again yesterday.

00:10:54.519 --> 00:10:56.288
-The country's doing the best
it's ever done.

00:10:56.288 --> 00:10:59.591
And I just heard that
she'd like to impeach.

00:10:59.591 --> 00:11:01.927
Our country's doing
the best it's ever done.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:03.195
They're going to lose
the election,

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:05.063
and they figure
this is a thing to do.

00:11:05.063 --> 00:11:07.933
This never happened where
we're in the election.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:10.001
And, I mean, if she does that,

00:11:10.001 --> 00:11:13.205
they all say that's a positive
for me from the election.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.606
You could also say,
"Who needs it?

00:11:14.606 --> 00:11:15.975
It's bad for the country."

00:11:15.975 --> 00:11:18.444
-Of course, his first priority
is, "It's good for me."

00:11:18.444 --> 00:11:20.211
And then he throws in
as an afterthought,

00:11:20.211 --> 00:11:21.880
"Also, it's bad
for the country."

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.216
He's like an athlete
who bet against his own team.

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:26.118
"Yes, the Patriots
scored a touchdown!

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:30.789
I mean, damn, let's go, Jets."

00:11:30.789 --> 00:11:33.225
The reality is that
if we finally have

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:36.729
a real formal impeachment
process with hearings and votes,

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:38.697
we'll all get to see
actual evidence

00:11:38.697 --> 00:11:41.033
of Trump's serial corruption
and lawbreaking

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.068
live on national television
every single day.

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:44.103
And that's a huge deal.

00:11:44.103 --> 00:11:45.704
Now, just before
we taped this show,

00:11:45.704 --> 00:11:47.172
Trump held another
of his signature

00:11:47.172 --> 00:11:48.573
off-the-rails press conferences

00:11:48.573 --> 00:11:51.343
where he once again lost his
mind on national television.

00:11:51.343 --> 00:11:53.779
First he started out by claiming
the whistle-blower

00:11:53.779 --> 00:11:56.648
who reported on his conversation
with the president of Ukraine

00:11:56.648 --> 00:11:59.251
didn't have what he called
first-class information,

00:11:59.251 --> 00:12:01.553
although it was hard to follow
what he was saying.

00:12:01.553 --> 00:12:03.188
-The so-called whistle-blower,

00:12:03.188 --> 00:12:08.727
the one that didn't have
any first-class or first-rate

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:13.765
or second-tier information,
from what I understand.

00:12:13.765 --> 00:12:15.601
You'll have to figure that out
for yourself.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.736
-Firsthand!

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:20.973
He didn't have any
firsthand information!

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:22.240
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:25.944
"First-rate, first-class.

00:12:25.944 --> 00:12:32.217
Didn't have any
first-base information.

00:12:32.217 --> 00:12:35.754
The common phrase,
first-base information."

00:12:35.754 --> 00:12:37.956
I mean, why does he make us
try to figure out

00:12:37.956 --> 00:12:39.691
what the hell
he's trying to say?

00:12:39.691 --> 00:12:41.159
"You'll have to figure out
what I'm --

00:12:41.159 --> 00:12:44.063
I'll say words, then you guys
put them into sentences."

00:12:44.063 --> 00:12:45.998
[ Laughter ]

00:12:45.998 --> 00:12:48.033
Then Trump complained
that because everyone

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.035
was talking about Ukraine
and impeachment,

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:52.037
no one was covering
how hard he was working

00:12:52.037 --> 00:12:53.972
during his meetings
with foreign leaders.

00:12:53.972 --> 00:12:57.309
-The sad thing about this hoax
is that we work so hard

00:12:57.309 --> 00:12:59.210
with all of these countries.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.180
And, I mean, really hard.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:05.050
I've been up from early in the
morning to late in the evening

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.453
and meeting with
different countries,

00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:08.887
all for the good of our country,

00:13:08.887 --> 00:13:11.257
and the press doesn't even cover
all of this.

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:13.158
-Early in the mornings
and late in --

00:13:13.158 --> 00:13:17.129
So you mean a workday.
You had a workday.

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:21.166
"We start in the morning.
And then we stop for lunch.

00:13:21.166 --> 00:13:23.635
It's called a lunch break.
First I've heard of it.

00:13:23.635 --> 00:13:25.237
Then we have meetings again
at night.

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:28.574
I'm working like eight,
nine hours a day."

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:30.108
[ Laughter ]

00:13:30.108 --> 00:13:31.710
Trump wants us all
to be impressed

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.778
by how hard the job is.

00:13:32.778 --> 00:13:34.045
But we knew it was hard.

00:13:34.045 --> 00:13:35.814
You're like the only one
who was like,

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:38.918
"Presidents work mornings?"

00:13:38.918 --> 00:13:41.954
What we saw in today's memo
alone is impeachable behavior,

00:13:41.954 --> 00:13:44.222
and Trump and his lawyer
keep going on TV

00:13:44.222 --> 00:13:45.824
and confessing to more crimes.

00:13:45.824 --> 00:13:47.526
When it comes to corruption
and lawlessness,

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:48.593
what we saw today was...

00:13:48.593 --> 00:13:51.696
-Absolutely a 10.
It was perfect.

00:13:51.696 --> 00:13:53.098
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:53.098 --> 00:13:55.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

